---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { ADS_ON } from '../lib/site';
---
<Page title="Cookie policy" description="Which cookies fbatactics.com uses: none of its own, and Google advertising cookies only once ads are enabled — with consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland." kicker="Legal" updated="November 8, 2026">
  <h2>Cookies set by this site</h2><p>None. There is no login, analytics, comments, newsletter or preference storage. Calculators, search, checklists and the knowledge check keep what you enter only in the open page.</p>
  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Google AdSense</td><td>Serving and measuring ads; personalization where you allow it; fraud prevention</td><td>{ADS_ON ? 'Active' : 'Not active — no ad code runs until approval and switch-on'}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Google consent message</td><td>Records consent choices for the EEA, UK and Switzerland</td><td>{ADS_ON ? 'Active in those regions' : 'Not active'}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GitHub Pages</td><td>Hosts the files; sets no cookies on this site</td><td>Active</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h2>Your choices</h2><p>Block or delete cookies in your browser. Once ads are active, visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland can change consent from the privacy settings link on the page, and anyone can manage personalized ads at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>. Details: <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</Page>
